.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
.Dd October 11, 2026
.Dt DTFL_STREAM_SCOPE 3
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm dtfl_stream_scope ,
.Nm dtfl_stream_type ,
.Nm dtfl_message_time ,
.Nm dtfl_message_len ,
.Nm dtfl_message_record
.Nd timely dataflow streams and the messages on them
.Sh LIBRARY
Timely and differential dataflow library
.Pq libdtfl , \-ldtfl
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In dtfl/timely.h
.Ft dtfl_scope *
.Fn dtfl_stream_scope "const dtfl_stream *st"
.Ft "const dtfl_type *"
.Fn dtfl_stream_type "const dtfl_stream *st"
.Ft "const uint64_t *"
.Fn dtfl_message_time "const dtfl_message *m"
.Ft size_t
.Fn dtfl_message_len "const dtfl_message *m"
.Ft "const void *"
.Fn dtfl_message_record "const dtfl_message *m" "size_t i" "size_t *len"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
A stream is a handle to an operator output.
It carries messages, each a timestamp and a batch of records, to the
operators that take it as input.
Streams are small handles owned by their scope; the user need not free
them.
.Pp
.Fn dtfl_stream_scope
returns the scope that contains
.Fa st ,
and
.Fn dtfl_stream_type
the record type its messages carry.
.Pp
A message is read inside operator logic through
.Xr dtfl_op_input_next 3 .
.Fn dtfl_message_time
returns its timestamp, a vector of the scope's time class.
.Fn dtfl_message_len
returns the number of records, and
.Fn dtfl_message_record
returns record
.Fa i
and stores its length in
.Fa *len .
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Fn dtfl_stream_scope
returns the containing scope and
.Fn dtfl_stream_type
the record type.
.Fn dtfl_message_time
returns the time words,
.Fn dtfl_message_len
the record count, and
.Fn dtfl_message_record
a pointer to record
.Fa i .
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
dtfl_message *m = dtfl_op_input_next(op, 0);
if (m != NULL) {
	const uint64_t *t = dtfl_message_time(m);
	size_t i, n = dtfl_message_len(m);
	for (i = 0; i < n; i++) {
		size_t len;
		const void *rec = dtfl_message_record(m, i, &len);
		/* ... use rec ... */
	}
}
.Ed
.Sh ERRORS
These accessors do not return error codes.
A record index at or beyond
.Fn dtfl_message_len
is out of range.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr dtfl_op_builder_new 3 ,
.Xr dtfl_op_input_next 3 ,
.Xr dtfl_pact_pipeline 3 ,
.Xr dtfl_scope_scoped 3
.Sh HISTORY
These are the C forms of timely's
.Vt Stream
.Pq stream.rs
and its
.Vt Message
.Pq channels/mod.rs .
.Sh THREAD SAFETY
A stream and the messages read from it belong to the worker thread that
builds and runs the dataflow and must not be shared.
